WEBVTT

00:00:09.032 --> 00:00:30.800
Chapter 1. A Young Man's Dream

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:36.276
My story begins in the 1630s.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:41.080
It is the time of the Ottoman Empire.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:49.796
Hezarfen Ahmet Çelebi is a clever young man of those days.

00:00:49.856 --> 00:00:57.511
He lives in the district of Üsküdar in Istanbul.

00:00:57.571 --> 00:01:04.555
Every morning, Hezarfen sits near the Bosphorus Strait.

00:01:04.616 --> 00:01:13.130
He looks at the tall tower in the district of Galata, across the water.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:20.574
The Galata Tower is taller than all the buildings near it.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:23.206
Simit!

00:01:23.265 --> 00:01:26.622
Would you like a simit?

00:01:26.682 --> 00:01:30.468
A man near Hezarfen calls.

00:01:30.528 --> 00:01:36.352
He has some tasty Turkish bread rings on his head.

00:01:36.412 --> 00:01:41.175
But Hezarfen doesn't answer.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:48.688
Every morning the man cries, Would you like a simit?

00:01:48.748 --> 00:01:53.607
But Hezarfen never answers.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:58.444
He doesn't hear or see the man.

00:01:58.504 --> 00:02:01.744
He is dreaming.

00:02:01.804 --> 00:02:10.766
In his dream, he is flying over the Bosphorus with the sea birds.

00:02:10.826 --> 00:02:17.547
One day, I want to look down from the sky on Istanbul.

00:02:17.607 --> 00:02:24.236
He thinks, I want to fly across the strait with you, birds.

00:02:24.296 --> 00:02:39.500
But how?

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:04.306
Chapter 2. Drawings from Italy. 

00:03:04.406 --> 00:03:10.406
Weeks later, Hezarfen is near the Bosphorus again.

00:03:10.466 --> 00:03:17.088
Again, he is looking carefully up at the sea birds in the sky.

00:03:17.148 --> 00:03:23.771
These days, he is making some big wings in his workshop.

00:03:23.831 --> 00:03:28.000
He needs some help with the design.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.942
Hezarfen! Someone calls.
  
00:03:32.002 --> 00:03:38.666
Hezarfen sees his friend, Mehmet, with a second man.

00:03:38.726 --> 00:03:43.350
He goes over and says hello to the two of them.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.621
Hezarfen, this is my brother Ali.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:55.164
Mehmet says, he's got some drawings for you from Italy.

00:03:55.224 --> 00:04:03.068
They're old drawings of birds' wings by Leonardo da Vinci.

00:04:03.128 --> 00:04:04.900
Ali says.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:10.132
Ah, yes. I know Leonardo's work.
 
00:04:10.192 --> 00:04:12.213
Hezarfen says.

00:04:12.273 --> 00:04:15.004
Let's see them then.

00:04:15.064 --> 00:04:19.477
Ali gives the drawings to Hezarfen.

00:04:19.536 --> 00:04:22.670
He looks at them for a minute.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:27.146
Interesting, Hezarfen says.

00:04:27.206 --> 00:04:29.967
Then he gives them back.

00:04:30.027 --> 00:04:33.529
Thank you, Ali.

00:04:33.589 --> 00:04:43.185
Days later, in Hezarfen's workshop, my wings are ready.

00:04:43.245 --> 00:04:46.355
Hezarfen tells his friends.

00:04:46.415 --> 00:04:51.595
Let's see you fly then, Mehmet cries.

00:04:51.655 --> 00:04:57.838
Your brother Lagari wants to fly too, I hear.

00:04:57.898 --> 00:04:59.960
Ali says.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.982
Everyone in Istanbul knows that.

00:05:05.042 --> 00:05:12.345
Yes, everybody's talking about him these days, I hear.

00:05:12.405 --> 00:05:16.812
But he isn't interested in wings.

00:05:16.871 --> 00:05:23.020
He wants to make a rocket. Hezarfen answers.
 
00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:28.966
So, where do you want to practice? Mehmet asks.
 
00:05:29.025 --> 00:05:35.261
There's a hill, not far from here. Hezarfen says.
 
00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.200
I can practice there.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:45.500
Hezarfen and Mehmet go up to the top of the hill.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.858
Ali waits at the foot of it.
 
00:05:49.918 --> 00:05:55.000
Mehmet helps Hezarfen with his wings.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:06:00.782
Then he looks down. Hey!
 
00:06:00.842 --> 00:06:04.974
Don't jump from here, he says.

00:06:05.034 --> 00:06:07.525
It's dangerous.

00:06:07.585 --> 00:06:09.966
But I must!

00:06:10.026 --> 00:06:12.409
Hezarfen says.

00:06:12.469 --> 00:06:18.157
My brother is beginning work on his rocket now.

00:06:18.217 --> 00:06:22.752
But I want to fly first.

00:06:22.812 --> 00:06:27.898
Then he runs and jumps.

00:06:27.958 --> 00:06:46.000
Mehmet closes his eyes.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:07:09.700
Chapter 3. To Galata.
 
00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:13.226
Hezarfen doesn’t fly.

00:07:13.285 --> 00:07:16.008
He falls.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:26.396
Mehmet hears a big crash and a cry from the foot of the hill.

00:07:26.456 --> 00:07:31.891
He goes quickly down the hill to his friend.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:37.448
Hezarfen is lying under his wings.

00:07:37.508 --> 00:07:40.898
Ali is next to him.

00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:49.020
His leg’s broken. Ali says. No, it isn't.
  
00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.901
Hezarfen answers.

00:07:51.961 --> 00:07:57.422
My wings are broken, but I'm okay.

00:07:57.482 --> 00:08:02.150
This time. Mehmet cries.
 
00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:06.108
But what about next time?

00:08:06.168 --> 00:08:09.008
Be careful, my friend.

00:08:09.068 --> 00:08:12.409
You don't want to die.

00:08:12.469 --> 00:08:20.130
They take the broken wings back to Hezarfen's workshop.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:25.000
Now what, Ali asks?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.893
I understand more.

00:08:28.953 --> 00:08:37.846
The design of my wings needs to be different, bigger and better.

00:08:37.906 --> 00:08:43.347
But that can wait, as our friend says.

00:08:43.407 --> 00:08:51.319
Right now, I must go and see the District Chief of Galata.

00:08:51.379 --> 00:08:55.430
Galata? Mehmet cries.
 
00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.285
Why?

00:08:57.345 --> 00:09:01.982
I want to fly from the Galata Tower.

00:09:02.042 --> 00:09:05.815
So I need his permission for that.

00:09:05.874 --> 00:09:08.036
Forget it.

00:09:08.096 --> 00:09:15.090
The District Chief never asks people into his office.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.191
Ali says.

00:09:17.251 --> 00:09:19.500
Let's see.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.214
Hezarfen cries.

00:09:22.274 --> 00:09:24.127
Come on.

00:09:24.187 --> 00:09:32.695
He and his friends take a boat across the Bosphorus.

00:09:32.755 --> 00:09:42.552
The three friends walk from the Bosphorus up to the Galata Tower.

00:09:42.612 --> 00:09:48.786
Two tall guards stop them when they arrive.

00:09:48.846 --> 00:09:51.058
What do you want?

00:09:51.118 --> 00:09:53.212
One of them asks.

00:09:53.272 --> 00:09:58.670
We want to see the District Chief of Galata.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.642
Hezarfen answers.

00:10:01.702 --> 00:10:05.788
Ali and Mehmet are afraid.

00:10:05.848 --> 00:10:10.903
What's your name? The guard asks.
 
00:10:10.963 --> 00:10:15.476
Hezarfen Ahmet Çelebi.

00:10:15.536 --> 00:10:25.176
Ah, the brother of the rocket maker, Lagari Hasan Çelebi.

00:10:25.236 --> 00:10:29.777
All Istanbul is talking of him.

00:10:29.837 --> 00:10:38.289
The guard says, yes, Hezarfen answers tiredly.

00:10:38.349 --> 00:10:43.320
So, can I see the district chief?

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:46.052
He asks the man.

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:47.775
Wait!

00:10:47.835 --> 00:11:10.700
The guard says, and he goes into the District Chief's office.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:34.200
Chapter 4. A Brother's Help.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:43.983
Sometime later, the guard takes Hezarfen to the District Chief's office.

00:11:44.044 --> 00:11:49.968
Mehmet and Ali wait at the door.

00:11:50.028 --> 00:11:57.046
The District Chief listens to Hezarfen's story.

00:11:57.106 --> 00:12:02.009
Very well. He smiles.
 
00:12:02.069 --> 00:12:06.300
You can fly from the tower.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:09.812
But be careful.

00:12:09.872 --> 00:12:14.413
Don't fall and die.

00:12:14.473 --> 00:12:21.445
No, District Chief. Hezarfen answers.
 
00:12:21.505 --> 00:12:28.384
And I'd like to see your brother. Tell him.
 
00:12:28.444 --> 00:12:35.817
Yes, District Chief. Hezarfen says.
 
00:12:35.877 --> 00:12:40.390
I've got permission!

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:45.906
Hezarfen laughs when he comes out into the street.

00:12:45.966 --> 00:12:50.148
Good! Ali cries happily.
 
00:12:50.208 --> 00:12:54.802
What now? Mehmet asks.
 
00:12:54.863 --> 00:13:01.802
I must visit Lagari. Hezarfen says.
 
00:13:01.863 --> 00:13:08.438
So Hezarfen visits his older brother.

00:13:08.498 --> 00:13:16.514
Lagari is working on his rocket when Hezarfen arrives.

00:13:16.574 --> 00:13:22.433
Nice design. Hezarfen says.
 
00:13:22.493 --> 00:13:26.219
Yes, Lagari answers.

00:13:26.279 --> 00:13:33.630
Perhaps early next year, I can fly up into the sky in it.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:35.651
What about you?

00:13:35.711 --> 00:13:38.111
Me, brother.

00:13:38.171 --> 00:13:46.623
I want to fly across the sky with my wings later this year.

00:13:46.683 --> 00:13:53.504
So, it's a race. Lagari laughs.
 
00:13:53.564 --> 00:13:57.655
Yes, Hezarfen smiles.

00:13:57.715 --> 00:14:04.927
But listen, the District Chief of Galata wants to see you.

00:14:04.987 --> 00:14:10.008
Right, well, thank you for your visit.

00:14:10.068 --> 00:14:14.020
Good luck with your wings, Hezarfen.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:18.181
Good luck with your rocket, Lagari.

00:14:18.241 --> 00:14:23.010
And Hezarfen leaves.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:31.302
Two weeks later, Hezarfen's new wings are ready.

00:14:31.362 --> 00:14:37.086
Now I can fly from Galata to Üsküdar.

00:14:37.146 --> 00:14:39.168
He cries.

00:14:39.228 --> 00:14:41.028
Wait!

00:14:41.088 --> 00:14:46.296
You must ask the Sultan's permission for that, I think.

00:14:46.356 --> 00:14:48.292
Mehmet says.

00:14:48.352 --> 00:14:55.768
And the Sultan says no to most people when they ask for things.

00:14:55.828 --> 00:15:02.114
So what can I do? Hezarfen cries.
 
00:15:02.174 --> 00:15:13.478
Listen, these days the District Chief of Galata talks about your brother a lot.

00:15:13.538 --> 00:15:19.488
Now, the sultan's interested in him too.

00:15:19.548 --> 00:15:29.238
Perhaps, Lagari can ask the sultan for a meeting, Ali says.

00:15:29.298 --> 00:15:36.312
So, Hezarfen goes and speaks to his brother again.

00:15:36.373 --> 00:15:43.300
Yes, I can ask the Sultan, Lagari smiles, 

00:15:43.360 --> 00:16:03.900
but he can always say no to a meeting.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:28.800
Chapter 5. What does the Sultan say?

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:33.072
So, Lagari speaks to the Sultan.

00:16:33.132 --> 00:16:38.404
And the Sultan says yes to a meeting.

00:16:38.464 --> 00:16:45.666
Seven days later, Hezarfen goes to the palace.

00:16:45.726 --> 00:16:50.288
He walks past the Hagia Sophia.

00:16:50.348 --> 00:16:53.129
He is nervous.

00:16:53.189 --> 00:16:58.983
Please give me permission. He thinks.
 
00:16:59.043 --> 00:17:02.216
near the Blue Mosque.

00:17:02.276 --> 00:17:05.297
He is more nervous.

00:17:05.358 --> 00:17:11.070
Please say yes. He thinks.
 
00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:16.272
Hezarfen stops near the palace.

00:17:16.332 --> 00:17:21.564
The Sultan can of course say no.

00:17:21.625 --> 00:17:27.747
Or worse, he can say, kill that man.

00:17:27.807 --> 00:17:30.263
He thinks.

00:17:30.323 --> 00:17:34.920
I'm Hezarfen Ahmet Çelebi.

00:17:34.981 --> 00:17:38.302
The Sultan wants to see me.

00:17:38.362 --> 00:17:41.686
He tells the palace guard.

00:17:41.746 --> 00:17:44.817
The man goes in.

00:17:44.878 --> 00:17:48.079
Hezarfen waits.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:52.483
He is very nervous now.

00:17:52.543 --> 00:17:58.166
After an hour, the guard comes back.

00:17:58.226 --> 00:18:00.196
Come with me.

00:18:00.256 --> 00:18:03.814
He says to Hezarfen.

00:18:03.874 --> 00:18:12.346
Hezarfen bows very nervously when he meets the Sultan.

00:18:12.406 --> 00:18:20.120
Your Highness, I want to fly across the Bosphorus.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:25.682
He says, the Sultan smiles.

00:18:25.742 --> 00:18:28.030
Ah yes.

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:35.100
You’re Lagari Hasan’s brother, he says.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:41.442
Yes, Your Highness, Hezarfen answers.

00:18:41.502 --> 00:18:47.324
Then he asks for the sultan's permission.

00:18:47.384 --> 00:18:50.526
You have it.

00:18:50.586 --> 00:18:53.007
The sultan says.

00:18:53.067 --> 00:18:59.582
You must fly across the Bosphorus tomorrow.

00:18:59.642 --> 00:19:05.186
With a good wind, Hezarfen says.

00:19:05.246 --> 00:19:11.130
But without it, what then your highness?

00:19:11.191 --> 00:19:16.074
You must ask God for a wind.

00:19:16.134 --> 00:19:18.947
The Sultan smiles.

00:19:19.007 --> 00:19:21.693
Your highness.

00:19:21.753 --> 00:19:32.864
A vizier says quietly, people can walk with their legs, but we don't have wings.

00:19:32.924 --> 00:19:39.198
Is a flying man good in God's eyes?

00:19:39.259 --> 00:19:44.192
Listen, the Sultan answers.

00:19:44.252 --> 00:19:49.048
We can think of new things with our brains.

00:19:49.108 --> 00:19:52.582
And our brains come from God.

00:19:52.642 --> 00:19:59.218
The first flying man must be an Ottoman, I say.

00:19:59.278 --> 00:20:02.340
Yes, Your Highness.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:04.832
The vizier says.

00:20:04.892 --> 00:20:10.306
But he looks angrily at Hezarfen.

00:20:10.366 --> 00:20:16.210
That evening, Hezarfen is not happy.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:19.231
There's no wind.

00:20:19.291 --> 00:20:37.500
He tells Mehmet and Ali.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:21:01.500
Chapter 6. Hezarfen’s Reward.
 
00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:07.191
The next morning, there is lots of wind.

00:21:07.251 --> 00:21:16.453
Hezarfen stands happily with his wings at the top of the Galata Tower.

00:21:16.514 --> 00:21:23.316
Suddenly, he jumps. He's falling!
 
00:21:23.376 --> 00:21:29.471
People cry, but he is not falling.

00:21:29.532 --> 00:21:41.250
He is flying with his big, white wings over the houses of Galata.

00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:52.578
Hezarfen’s friends, Mehmet and Ali, run with the people down the streets to the Bosphorus.

00:21:52.638 --> 00:21:58.653
Hezarfen flies out over the water.

00:21:58.713 --> 00:22:04.338
I'm flying! He cries.
 
00:22:04.398 --> 00:22:08.470
People can fly!

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:17.350
He lands across the strait in Üsküdar, a happy man.

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:27.530
The next day, the Sultan has a meeting with his viziers at the palace.

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:31.652
People can fly.

00:22:31.712 --> 00:22:34.200
He cries excitedly.

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:41.108
And the first flying man is an Ottoman.

00:22:41.168 --> 00:22:45.560
That's good for our empire.

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:50.592
Hezarfen needs a reward.

00:22:50.652 --> 00:22:57.200
But your highness, the vizier, nearest to him, says.

00:22:57.300 --> 00:23:04.473
Flying men can land in our palaces and kill us.

00:23:04.533 --> 00:23:08.306
They're dangerous.

00:23:08.366 --> 00:23:13.951
The Sultan thinks about this.

00:23:14.011 --> 00:23:18.766
Yes, I see.

00:23:18.826 --> 00:23:21.888
Perhaps you're right.

00:23:21.948 --> 00:23:28.271
So, what must we do with Hezarfen then?

00:23:28.331 --> 00:23:30.512
He asks.

00:23:30.572 --> 00:23:36.094
Kill him. The Vizier answers.
 
00:23:36.154 --> 00:23:39.996
I can't do that.

00:23:40.056 --> 00:23:42.658
The Sultan cries.

00:23:42.718 --> 00:23:46.629
Then, exile him.

00:23:46.689 --> 00:23:50.514
The Vizier says.

00:23:50.575 --> 00:24:00.212
And so the Sultan calls Hezarfen Ahmet Çelebi to the palace.

00:24:00.272 --> 00:24:06.866
He gives a reward of a thousand gold coins to him.

00:24:06.926 --> 00:24:12.970
Then he exiles him to Algeria.

00:24:13.030 --> 00:24:21.322
Hezarfen says goodbye to his brother and his friends.

00:24:21.382 --> 00:24:26.542
He leaves Istanbul that evening.

00:24:26.602 --> 00:24:36.156
After that, he can fly over the Bosphorus with the birds in his dreams.

00:24:36.216 --> 00:24:43.228
But he can never go back to Istanbul again.

00:24:43.288 --> 00:24:48.150
And what about Lagari and his rocket?

00:24:48.210 --> 00:24:50.587
You ask.

00:24:50.648 --> 00:25:15.000
Well, perhaps one day, I can tell you that story too.